
1. Requirement Gathering	5 min	Clarify scope, functional and non-functional requirements
2. Core Entities & Relationships	7 min	Identify entities, attributes, and relationships
3. Class Design	8 min	Define classes, interfaces, methods, and responsibilities
4. Workflows & Design Patterns	7 min	Explain key workflows and justify design patterns
5. UML Diagram	5 min	Draw class diagrams and show relationships
6. Edge Cases & Design	5 min	Handle failures, concurrency, validation, and extensibility
7. Implementation & Coding	8 min	Implement core classes and demonstrate the main workflow
Total	45 min	Complete the LLD interview


1. Requirement Gathering: Functional requirements, non-functional requirements, scope, assumptions, and clarifying questions.
2. Core Entities & Relationships: Entities, attributes, associations, cardinality, inheritance, composition, and aggregation.
3. Class Design: Classes, objects, constructors, methods, interfaces, abstract classes, encapsulation, and SOLID principles.
4. Workflows & Design Patterns: Use cases, sequence of operations, Strategy, Factory, Observer, and State patterns.
5. UML Diagram: Class diagrams, sequence diagrams, association, inheritance, composition, aggregation, and multiplicity.
6. Edge Cases & Design: Validation, exceptions, concurrency, race conditions, extensibility, and separation of concerns.



Implementation & Coding: Folder structure, interfaces, concrete classes, service classes, repositories, enums, and executable workflows.
